# <PROJECT_NAME> — Glossary (one name per concept)

> This file is a RULE, not a nicety. Two words for one thing shipped a production bug: a lookup took
> the new meaning of a word, searched where the old meaning lived, matched nothing, and an empty
> match silently widened a filter to the whole dataset (Pitfall 31). Name each concept exactly once,
> and name where each subsystem carries it. **Adding a fifth name for an existing concept is a
> defect.** Rename only while already editing the file that carries the wrong name, and say so in
> the commit.

